-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Jilly's Farm Volume 1 - SokoBAArn!
  Publisher   Bob's Stuff, 2017
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Jilly's Farm Volume 1 - SokoBAArn! (2017)(Bob's Stuff).tap
  MD5         86a5e1dc43e4cfe45582e91eb7cd1cf3

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

  Memory      Any Next: a 1MB Next has the memory for the game. Enhanced needs
              a 1MB Next, and is not offered on a smaller one.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  The game's play area has no colour clash, so none is removed: the default
  keeps the original look. The patch adds the menu and the Next start-up. Game
  logic is unchanged. Enhanced colours, an option on the menu, are below.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    The Spec256 set by Ynicky, faithfully, on a Layer 2 that holds
              the set's colour values, with a second buffer as the game has
              one, so masked figures stay whole. Every coloured byte of the
              V1.00 set matches this V1.01 release 13 bytes higher; nothing
              went without. Value FF shows the ULA below in the cell's own
              colours. Source: Enhanced colours: Ynicky (Spec256).

  Pace        original (+0.65% measured in JNext 1.1.104, against the original
              on a 48K machine, game state in lockstep)

  Changes     1.0: the original game with Sinclair's 48K ROM as the whole alt
              ROM (NextZXOS 26.11 safe); no game byte changed, no hook in the
              default; the tape's own loading screen; Enhanced, the Spec256
              colours faithfully, mapped by graphic from V1.00, off by default

  Note        Keys: menu 0 start, 1 keyboard, 2 rotational, 3 define keys, 4
              level code, 5 level editor. Z, K, M, X move the sheep, L undo, Q
              quit. Default: the original game, picture and all; it never had
              colour clash. Enhanced (off by default): the Spec256 colours as
              they are; the set is V1.00, this release V1.01, so colours are
              mapped by graphic. Fits 1MB. Known issues: pace in JNext against
              the original, Enhanced, 7 runs of 3,000 updates over 3 levels,
              state in lockstep: whole runs -0.35 to +0.85%, quiet thirds
              -0.04 to +1.17%, busy thirds -1.59 to +0.30%, slowest 20 updates
              +6.99%, fastest -6.54%; default: 0.00%, no hook; Enhanced, as on
              Spec256: the sheep's painted face shows only in the routine that
              doesn't shift it, and the level editor's blue cursor can't be
              seen. Missing: no cheats (the archive has no .pok for this
              release); natural play to the end (levels reached by the game's
              own codes); the level editor and Sinclair or redefined keys not
              played in a long run; hardware untested.

