-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Run by script through the real loader on a NextZXOS 26.11 card
              copy, default and Enhanced; 1.0 not yet played by the owner;
              published at his request

  Replay      Enhanced: 4 scripted recordings (a clean run; all 30 levels by
              the game's own codes; 2 in the level editor), 36741 frames:
              263813 hooks run original and build from one state each: every
              register including R, all 48K RAM but 32 bytes of dead stack:
              IDENTICAL; 109114 value buffers and 39301 Layer 2 pictures
              against an independent model running the set's plane bytes
              through the game's own byte operations, whose master plane must
              equal the game's real buffer: IDENTICAL; 13 broken builds
              caught; 1792 ABI cases, each hook entered at all 4 CPU speeds,
              both IFF values, 8 R phases; the start-up exact with and without
              NEXLOAD. Default: no hook, the v1.0 proof stands, its bytes
              unchanged

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless: through the real .NEXCLASH loader on a
              private NextZXOS 26.11 card copy, from the tape, default and
              Enhanced, output byte for byte as nxc.py makes it, reaching
              play; 15-minute soak against the original and flicker check on
              Enhanced, clean; exact Enhanced frames of levels 1, 6, 14, 23
              against the set in emuspec256: differences only a colour nudged
              off the transparent value and the two emulators' greys

  Coverage    Scripted input, no human play: menu, levels 1 and 2 by play, all
              30 levels by the game's own codes, the level editor by random
              keys; not reached: natural completion, redefined keys, the
              rotational controls; 8 hook sites never ran (same hooks as sites
              that did; the two hooks no recording reached, 93D4 and 96EB,
              tested by hand against the original): 70B0 A85D A864 A9B4 A9C8
              A9D2 A9DD A9E8

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
